          "url": "https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2023_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12",
          "question": "For complex number $u = a+bi$ and $v = c+di$ (where $i=\\sqrt{-1}$), define the binary operation\n$u \\otimes v = ac + bdi$\nSuppose $z$ is a complex number such that $z\\otimes z = z^{2}+40$. What is $|z|^2$?",
          "model_outputs": [
            "To solve this problem, we need to find the value of $|z|^2$ for a complex number $z$ such that $z\\otimes z = z^{2}+40$.\n\n1. **Understanding the given equation:**\n   We are given that $z\\otimes z = z^{2}+40$. This equation can be rewritten as $z^{2} + 2z + 40 = 0$.\n\n2. **Setting the equation equal to zero:**\n   We can set the equation equal to zero to find the values of $z$ and $z^{2}$:\n   \\[\n   z^{2} + 2z + 40 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} + 2z + 40 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} + 2z + 40 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} + 2z = 40\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} + 2z = 40\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} = 40 - 2z\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} = 38\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z = \\pm \\frac{38}{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Finding the value of $z^{2}$:**\n   We can find the value of $z^{2}$ by substituting the value of $z$ into the equation:\n   \\[\n   z^{2} = \\frac{38}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z^{2} = 19\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z = \\pm \\frac{19}{2}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Finding the value of $|z|^2$:**\n   We can find the value of $|z|^2$ by taking the square root of both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   |z|^2 = \\sqrt{\\frac{19}{2}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   |z|^2 = \\sqrt{\\frac{19}{2}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   |z|^2 = \\frac{19}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   |z|^2 = \\frac{19}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   |z|^2 = \\boxed{\\frac{19}{2}}\n   \\]",
